{#-
  Phase 3C/3D: R2's DESIRED secondary DHCPv4/DHCPv6 server configuration --
  the "dhcp server" global config-mode block ONLY.

  Phase 3D integrated this fragment into the real push path: it is now
  `{% include %}`-d directly from templates/R2.cfg.j2 (guarded by
  `{% if dhcp is defined %}`), the same file master.py's push_eos()
  renders and pushes for every other device -- there is exactly ONE
  authoritative desired R2 configuration, not two independently applied
  templates. The companion `interface Vlan200 / dhcp server ipv4/ipv6`
  enable lines live directly in templates/R2.cfg.j2's OWN existing
  `interface Vlan200` stanza (not duplicated here as a second stanza) --
  see docs/NETBOX_IPAM.md "Phase 3D" for why. This file is also still
  rendered standalone by netbox/scripts/render_r2_dhcp.py for its
  narrower nested-grammar structural check (Step 11).

  Every address/pool value below comes from the `dhcp` context built by
  modules/ipam_context.build_and_validate_r2_dhcp_context() (itself
  sourced entirely from NetBox ipam.IPRange/Prefix/VLAN objects) -- nothing
  here is a literal pool boundary.

  EOS command grammar verified read-only against the live cEOS 4.36.2F
  image (CliPlugin/DhcpServerCli.py) -- see docs/NETBOX_IPAM.md "Phase 3C".
  Phase 3D additionally proved this exact candidate (including the
  Vlan200 enable lines) via a live, NEVER-COMMITTED EOS configuration
  session on R2 -- zero parser errors, and the session diff touched only
  the intended DHCP lines (see docs/NETBOX_IPAM.md "Phase 3D").
-#}
dhcp server
   lease time ipv4 0 days 8 hours 0 minutes
   lease time ipv6 0 days 8 hours 0 minutes
{% for pool in dhcp.ipv4_subnets %}
   subnet {{ pool.prefix }}
      name VLAN{{ pool.vlan }}-v4-secondary
      default-gateway {{ pool.gateway }}
      range {{ pool.start }} {{ pool.end }}
{% endfor %}
{% for pool in dhcp.ipv6_subnets %}
   subnet {{ pool.prefix }}
      name VLAN{{ pool.vlan }}-v6-secondary
      range {{ pool.start }} {{ pool.end }}
{% endfor %}
!
